# Crossfade - the plainest thing two decks can do.
#
# Every file in this folder is a transition. Copy one, change it, and the player picks it
# up next time it starts - no rebuild. Yours live in ~/.config/ytmplayer/transitions and
# override a built-in one of the same name.
#
# The fade length in settings is the span of the WHOLE move. Where the join falls inside it
# is decided here, by where the leaving track's fader reaches zero: at 0.5, so fifteen
# seconds is seven and a half either side of the end of the old track. The arriving track
# goes on opening up through the second half, which is what a hand would be doing.

name    Crossfade
note    equal-power fade, the join in the middle
align   free
tempo   free
power   free

# lane <deck> <control>, then one line per keyframe: <when> <value> <ease>
#   decks     out (the track leaving) | in (the track arriving)
#   controls  gain bass mid high lowpass highpass speed tempo
#   when      bar <n> | at <0..1>
#   ease      hold linear smooth power-down power-up
#
# power-down and power-up are a pair. Two overlapping tracks are uncorrelated, so their
# powers add, and this pair is what holds out^2 + in^2 at exactly one.

lane out gain
    at 0.0    1.0    power-down
    at 0.5    0.0    hold
    at 1.0    0.0    hold

lane in gain
    at 0.0    0.0    power-up
    at 0.5    1.0    hold
    at 1.0    1.0    hold

# The arriving track comes in with its bottom trimmed and opens out once it is alone, so
# the second half of the span is a recovery rather than padding.
lane in highpass
    at 0.0    220    smooth
    at 0.5    120    smooth
    at 0.85     0    hold
    at 1.0      0    hold
